irst  interest-free loans of 30 000 are by no  means cheap so can they work in time to  offset the additional costs an  increasingly older population will  produce to find an answer to that  question is a matter of time the reason  why europe may face a larger problem  with its dependency ratio than a country  like the united states besides the fact  that the us is younger generally is that  the eu's legitimacy is still more  precarious as a political institution  the eu schengen area made it possible  for europeans to move between borders  and is seen as an overall net positive  but the ability for europeans to move  freely between borders may also  exasperate pressures on the countries  that are facing an increasingly older  population rural regions continue to  decline in population while urban  regions continue to grow and this  phenomenon does not just happen within  countries but more importantly  concerning the stability of the entire  european union it happens between  countries within europe as there is an  outward migration of younger people to  urban centers due to better economic  opportunities central and eastern  european countries will continue to face  even more demographic pressure that can  weaken their economic growth and social  support systems and when that happens  enough for a long enough time that  people get increasingly concerned about  their younger neighbors leaving for  better economic opportunities elsewhere  the ramifications for the political  institution that seems like it is  accelerating that process can be huge  [Music]  you

